---
layout: layouts/base.njk
ogType: article
---
{#- Article layout. Sits on top of base.njk, so nav, footer, analytics and the
    hreflang machinery all come for free — an article declares a transKey the
    same way any other page does. UI strings come from site/_data/i18n.json. -#}
{%- set t = i18n[lang] -%}
<article>
  <header class="article-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="{{ site.languages[lang].home }}">{{ t.home }}</a> /
        <a href="{{ site.languages[lang].blog }}">{{ t.blogTitle }}</a> /
        {{ shortTitle or headline }}
      </p>
      {%- if category %}<span class="label">{{ category }}</span>{% endif %}
      <h1>{{ headline }}</h1>
      {%- if standfirst %}
      <p class="standfirst">{{ standfirst }}</p>
      {%- endif %}
      <p class="article-meta">
        <time datetime="{{ page.date | htmlDate }}">{{ page.date | postDate(lang) }}</time>
        {%- if readingTime %} · {{ readingTime }} {{ t.minRead }}{% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap article-body">
    {#- An article about a specific race points up at that race's page before
        its own body. The race page is the hub for the head query; the article
        is the depth. Nothing renders unless the article declares a raceId. -#}
    {%- if raceId %}{% include "partials/race-guide-link.njk" %}{% endif %}
    {{ content | safe }}
    {% include "partials/tool-cta.njk" %}
    {#- An article whose subject has a guide behind it trades that guide for an
        email. Same conditional shape as raceId above: nothing renders unless the
        article declares `toolCapture`, so this costs the other articles nothing.
        Added Sept 11, 2026 with the fuelling magnet — the three nutrition
        articles were the site's only public writing on a subject whose guide
        had just gone behind the paywall, and none of them captured anything. -#}
    {%- if toolCapture %}{% include "partials/tool-capture.njk" %}{% endif %}
  </div>
</article>

{#- Every article closes with the same offer. Defined once here so no article can
    forget it, and so changing the offer is one edit rather than one per article. -#}
<section class="article-cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="label">{{ t.ctaLabel }}</span>
    <h2>{{ t.ctaHeading }}</h2>
    <p>{{ t.ctaBody }}</p>
    <a href="{{ t.ctaHref }}" class="btn-primary">{{ t.ctaButton }}</a>
  </div>
</section>
